      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Intuitively, the Fourier Transform acts like a spectral analyst for a signal. Instead of looking at how the signal changes over *time*, it tells you *which frequencies* are present in that signal and how strong each one is. Imagine breaking a complex musical chord down into the individual notes—the Fourier Transform does that for waves. It transforms the signal from the time domain into the frequency domain.",
